Kernel_initialize
├── given the account has already been initialized
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitialization error
└── given the account has not been initialized
    ├── when packages array is empty
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidInitialization error
    └── when packages array has one or more elements
        ├── it should install all packages in order
        ├── given the first package is a validator
        │   ├── it should set the validator as the root
        │   ├── it should call onInstall on the validator
        │   └── it should emit ModuleInstalled and RootChanged events
        ├── given the first package is a permission
        │   ├── given there are both policy and signer packages
        │   │   ├── it should install the policies
        │   │   ├── it should install the signer
        │   │   └── it should set the permission as the root
        │   └── given the permission setup is incomplete
        │       └── it should revert with "Permission Install not finished"
        ├── given the first package is not a validator or permission
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidRootValidation error
        └── given subsequent packages contain executors hooks or fallbacks
            └── it should install all modules correctly
